  "summary": "Apache InLong manager-service is vulnerable to SQL injection through unvalidated ordering parameters",
  "details": "Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an SQL Command ('SQL Injection') vulnerability in Apache InLong. This allows an attacker to inject the string value into\nthe SQL statement, enabling SQL injection.\n\n\nThis issue affects Apache InLong: from 2.0.0 before 2.4.0.\n\n\n\nUsers are advised to upgrade to Apache InLong's  2.4.0 or cherry-pick [1] to solve it.\n\n[1]  https://github.com/apache/inlong/pull/12080 .",
